                        {
                          "id": "0974e2e4-85af-4d63-b7ba-ffcfe12fda60",
                          "text": "文档: Gadget for marking output parameters in type classes. For example, the `Members…",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "e166c86e-6131-4259-a64c-5e275324b19f",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\nGadget for marking output parameters in type classes.\n\nFor example, the `Membership` class is defined as:\n```\nclass Membership (α : outParam (Type u)) (γ : Type v)\n```\nThis means that whenever a typeclass goal of the form `Membership ?α ?γ` comes\nup, Lean will wait to solve it until `?γ` is known, but then it will run\ntypeclass inference, and take the first solution it finds, for any value of `?α`,\nwhich thereby determines what `?α` should be.\n\nThis expresses that in a term like `a ∈ s`, `s` might be a `Set α` or\n`List α` or some other type with a membership operation, and in each case\nthe \"member\" type `α` is determined by looking at the container type.",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "0d9690ea-557a-45e5-8ddf-afe604e4d0e4",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "5f74d9aa-ae85-4af7-87ad-46526d07547b",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 内部\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nSort u → Sort u\n```\n\n**文档**\nGadget for marking output parameters in type classes.\n\nFor example, the `Membership` class is defined as:\n```\nclass Membership (α : outParam (Type u)) (γ : Type v)\n```\nThis means that whenever a typeclass goal of the form `Membership ?α ?γ` comes\nup, Lean will wait to solve it until `?γ` is known, but then it will run\ntypeclass inference, and take the first solution it finds, for any value of `?α`,\nwhich thereby determines what `?α` should be.\n\nThis expresses that in a term like `a ∈ s`, `s` might be a `Set α` or\n`List α` or some other type with a membership operation, and in each case\nthe \"member\" type `α` is determined by looking at the container type.\n\n**说明** equation compiler / recursor / match 管道，默认折叠。",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "内部",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f9fafb",
                    "color": "#6b7280",
                    "fontSize": 12,
                    "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                  }
                },
